[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4049eacb-f333-5928-be15-ad4db6bd4e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474308} {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35601916-369e-51fe-abf4-791c123c637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474309} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b95782b-8b17-5f77-9801-8a99d11ccf2a" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e17bc7-fee0-5214-bbe1-e420ad24d8df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b8d5ec7-084e-5c9f-8f80-d0e39dff32c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474310} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a78c060-c106-55f9-a38d-38117b0a316f" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} {:answer/id #uuid "91b92ce5-41cb-5b8f-8a7e-42023c7326d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45cf437a-d3e6-5bff-a122-cc094f36db9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474312} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc403eaf-5b3a-598a-b3ae-28f5e22f4037" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130004" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-2y=0,$ where $x>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\right)+2x\\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(12{x}^{2})+2x(4{x}^{3})-2{x}^{4}=18{x}^{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution but ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6302f81d-4834-56a5-b014-0a97c3dccd6f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About General Solutions of Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} {:answer/id #uuid "91c226a9-4c73-5b94-92b0-1a733df3a834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4025a2da-8220-50a7-b4f3-219e6d29cc87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474302} :answer-field/id #uuid "f318ba66-ccb9-5f8e-9231-0f5fb32052aa" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb83e9ac-cb3a-5dc7-8842-0118c6b9c9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474304} {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74a023e8-6ba2-5b3f-a47a-189a8481e140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474305} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5c45ac-f6f4-5fdf-87b6-c55e5d17a5ea" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2a6d79-cf64-517d-a658-e230018451ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0e9691-308c-596d-9c85-fd9d5dd60a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474306} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a04d4f0-4217-55ed-ab79-e4478a4fd20e" :answer-field/key "The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-130000" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}-4y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =(1+x){e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =(2+x){e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n(2+x){e}^{x}-4(x{e}^{x})=(2-3x){e}^{x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation” is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x}-4{e}^{2x}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement “${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation” is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution while ${y}_{2}$ is a solution of the equation, hence $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement “The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a48276e-b920-56e8-b1be-c683e1a5049c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453898} {:answer/id #uuid "abced934-045e-5c93-a1c7-a8d4728d5f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a48276e-b920-56e8-b1be-c683e1a5049c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453898} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ab82079-7e85-5698-9d5f-f30535ae045b" :answer-field/key "$a\\cdot a<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c8a0d4-5a69-5540-a387-db4a6f42e8c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453900} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca7cff9-be90-50ca-b8fc-73dc0735fdfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c8a0d4-5a69-5540-a387-db4a6f42e8c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453900} :answer-field/id #uuid "eebfabe7-7839-5a6d-84e2-d01462259017" :answer-field/key "$b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e38cf291-0320-5c31-8186-438a6fd788ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453902} {:answer/id #uuid "8875f9e3-b96e-5b95-9de0-9e90087413bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8875f9e3-b96e-5b95-9de0-9e90087413bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453903} :answer-field/id #uuid "dabcc662-7340-592c-9a42-9679f674f7f3" :answer-field/key "$b\\cdot a=-2(a\\cdot a)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67" :question/math-academy-id "q-39207" :question/problem "Suppose $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $a\\cdot a<0$ is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$ is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-\\frac{1}{4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement $b\\cdot a=-2(a\\cdot a)$ is true. Simplifying the expression $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (4a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-4(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-2(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is $b\\cdot a=-2(a\\cdot a)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "395effed-4bfa-582d-b3e2-bbe356c7243d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453472} {:answer/id #uuid "621726bd-f7b9-5d1c-90ed-dd4a419d69d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "621726bd-f7b9-5d1c-90ed-dd4a419d69d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453473} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb064ed9-57d4-5777-8d35-09cf4b57705a" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "358ddacc-d123-58d8-925f-e9a4f0f35a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453474} {:answer/id #uuid "baf4e056-a6c9-5afa-bdb9-542a77805b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "358ddacc-d123-58d8-925f-e9a4f0f35a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453474} :answer-field/id #uuid "a978a13e-4c20-5a6d-b91d-7b677821d028" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227ac4ed-ec8b-55fd-a18c-e213264735bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453476} {:answer/id #uuid "6e59a1d7-c74a-566f-a558-8b5ff6c8e1c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "227ac4ed-ec8b-55fd-a18c-e213264735bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453476} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2e03518-33b3-5350-9a82-0e219b6dab78" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d743af0-a7a6-59cf-8a8b-38734a18e7f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-160458" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3x-1},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\le 0,$ we have $f(x)=3{e}^{3x-1}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{e}^{3x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3x-1}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}-0 \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is false. Since statement ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\le 0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba238c0a-584c-5ae7-a738-fc7794fd15bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453460} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4ad8a0-ddad-591e-ada0-ddaf6c95f293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4ad8a0-ddad-591e-ada0-ddaf6c95f293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453461} :answer-field/id #uuid "a40ef891-cc3c-51db-885c-7ec524281ffa" :answer-field/key "$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5f06e7f-7080-514c-b311-eef93e6db768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453462} {:answer/id #uuid "e37290c2-bc90-585f-bb57-e06daa169737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e37290c2-bc90-585f-bb57-e06daa169737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453463} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1678b1-1651-57aa-9ede-da2c2ed4ec4f" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74a4e92c-9f38-5f08-b27c-b20a2daf8744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453464} {:answer/id #uuid "f92c823f-dd97-5983-95bf-0ef1693de5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f92c823f-dd97-5983-95bf-0ef1693de5d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453465} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b23395f-4642-5914-969e-ff7e32133f85" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7af6cdaa-d1ff-562c-9d47-7e9a37adf5ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-160446" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function” is true. Since statements “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$” and ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$”; ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$; “$f(x)$ is a valid probability density function”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Horizontal Segment Under a Polar Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9148e7a1-c898-5010-a8da-e14468900021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474442} {:answer/id #uuid "8c509f0c-7869-50fd-97c8-0c39ad974d7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9148e7a1-c898-5010-a8da-e14468900021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474442} :answer-field/id #uuid "80fd21d2-d0e2-56a6-83b8-c52c5aa81167" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475147} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035981b4-173c-59ce-a4cc-935ef26ceb45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474444} {:answer/id #uuid "e09384a8-158b-5092-8870-775a085bfe39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e09384a8-158b-5092-8870-775a085bfe39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474445} :answer-field/id #uuid "a427db06-c7e8-5666-90dd-909a4adf6847" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475148} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33a494b7-3cef-5f9f-b5df-0019758840e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474446} {:answer/id #uuid "d9805b37-2717-5444-9336-eeda03de0a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9805b37-2717-5444-9336-eeda03de0a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474447} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5f8696b-5d50-5511-a270-5cccd6dc0050" :answer-field/key "The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $1$ centered at $O.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa0b27c3-d4dd-5c0c-8989-66af8729df06" :question/math-academy-id "q-161029" :question/problem "![](images/12/1252844f7a9e2fb2ca0ff1d2e2e1546a460e7d0846b4ae2996b6ce984ee305a1.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\le u\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ and $\\frac{1}{4}\\le u\\le 1.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right)),\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\le u\\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/49/49aa7d6ccd4b14b48ede7486f41ab11ac22b593c06d75795fe7819889b2b2f23.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “The image makes the angle of $0$ with the positive $x$-axis” is false, while statement “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ with the positive $x$-axis” is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right)}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement “The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $1$ centered at $O.$” is true.\n\n- When $u=\\frac{1}{4},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right),\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right)),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- When $u=1,$ we obtain the point \n$(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{12}\\right)),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $1.$\n\nSo, the endpoints of the line segment lie on the circles of radii $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}$ with the positive $x$-axis”; “The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $1$ centered at $O.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05739988-eeed-5afd-a445-e1dc677cc92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437840} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf029c1-b1a8-5a8b-a676-cd13b44e113b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05739988-eeed-5afd-a445-e1dc677cc92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437840} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4d7c78f-dac2-5b80-9554-1e05a93f2f93" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438949} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe246435-fd14-59a9-9160-df256f6ffb82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437842} {:answer/id #uuid "ff59cb0e-83ac-53c9-bb11-897ad674049d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff59cb0e-83ac-53c9-bb11-897ad674049d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437843} :answer-field/id #uuid "b39164a9-c699-5980-8ef6-6758528f95e7" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1885359c-b7e4-5e24-b124-f8d267e8840f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437844} {:answer/id #uuid "cccdf236-c391-54e1-b0dc-8e77683dd03d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1885359c-b7e4-5e24-b124-f8d267e8840f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437844} :answer-field/id #uuid "96047e81-3269-5f84-bfb2-854075b3c2f8" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c977abab-50be-5c44-961a-335884131fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437846} {:answer/id #uuid "209c01dc-3c0e-5ef6-b90f-25c2ce076ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c977abab-50be-5c44-961a-335884131fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437846} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ffbe2f7-9aa4-5310-9d23-ad54db885413" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5777673f-cba1-5775-ae01-f18d4531f239" :question/math-academy-id "q-131195" :question/problem "![](images/39/39dfec02c787141d8a728381f4093dfe9cbf3fdbf996177ba6f24d973015dc5f.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F>0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F=0$ and $∇\\cdot F<0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0743951f-f683-50d5-9001-7d4a2dc711a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437848} {:answer/id #uuid "893474df-f11f-5036-9840-620d813e6c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0743951f-f683-50d5-9001-7d4a2dc711a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437848} :answer-field/id #uuid "f75f2c7d-45a9-5c61-b5c3-f30297ac41ee" :answer-field/key "$∇\\cdot F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/r