wer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94d7c261-91e0-5aac-bbce-caaa5f7ca8a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437854} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d01df11-c07e-5e3b-a901-c578fe72ec74" :answer-field/key "$F$ is solenoidal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9278ec55-4908-5c1c-8a74-640611473537" :question/math-academy-id "q-131196" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4bf8de7e8719545b3d8abf5dc9fb4bc0c5f71034dba7186b7d9822d9e8be044d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F<0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F=0$ and $∇\\cdot F>0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $x$-components decrease as we move horizontally towards the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a sink at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F<0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} {:answer/id #uuid "d834568e-ce97-583c-8040-fc4e266d52c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14ecc36-432b-56ec-87ab-282eea355b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475002} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdad22ae-e385-521b-b788-7347685ca5ee" :answer-field/key "The temperature of a town on a certain day." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} {:answer/id #uuid "e8dfccef-97df-539d-8b11-97c54d234ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12cca481-ff11-55c7-91de-86d18673b2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475004} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c49dca-0d5f-5b4f-bddf-bbbd54a75e97" :answer-field/key "The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd75d4f-b796-573f-80aa-522e963beda1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09154e84-c363-5ed7-a1c0-e945e77a7a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475006} :answer-field/id #uuid "044a1424-5108-5da5-9fee-69fd6070dd31" :answer-field/key "The number of typos in a randomly selected book." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "239e34ce-3c73-5bae-b143-3d41bff8bf51" :question/math-academy-id "q-97754" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The temperature of a town on a certain day” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because a temperature is a real number, so the support is not finite.\n\n- Random variable “The number of letters of a word randomly selected from an English dictionary” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. Each outcome is not equally likely (there are more short words than very long words, for example).\n\n- Random variable “The number of typos in a randomly selected book” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the number of typos can be any positive integer. Moreover, each outcome is not equally likely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424377 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2527c71-4b45-56c5-ac1b-b9c3677ec446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474410} {:answer/id #uuid "538248d4-58af-5ebb-9766-95fbd02d680f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "538248d4-58af-5ebb-9766-95fbd02d680f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474411} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c6b22b2-16b6-594f-8629-233f8e4533ee" :answer-field/key "The number obtained when picking an integer between $0$ and $10$ at random." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530df43b-d990-5fd4-82d9-edd79acc72b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474412} {:answer/id #uuid "6023ed7f-25f2-56c5-ab2f-6510aa7999a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530df43b-d990-5fd4-82d9-edd79acc72b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474412} :answer-field/id #uuid "222f6d64-5b5d-5c46-9f01-2692fb7c4f99" :answer-field/key "The number obtained when picking a real number between $5$ and $9$ at random." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475132} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a6dcfb-7ab1-5090-9f90-e556d60b3df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474414} {:answer/id #uuid "a865cdfe-22a1-5062-a609-df9bcfa5289f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16a6dcfb-7ab1-5090-9f90-e556d60b3df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474414} :answer-field/id #uuid "d06fdfac-e110-5031-90bd-ef64919fe14d" :answer-field/key "The number of clients arriving at a shopping mall in a day." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78d51529-5603-5294-836c-698a99289cb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-148394" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can use the discrete uniform distribution to model the outcome of a single event when the support $S$ is finite, and each $x\\in S$ is equally likely.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable “The number obtained when picking an integer between $0$ and $10$ at random” can be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because there are a finite number of integers between $0$ and $10,$ and since the selection is random, each integer has an equal probability of being selected.\n\n- Random variable “The number obtained when picking a real number between $5$ and $9$ at random” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because there are infinitely many real numbers between $5$ and $9,$ and so the support is not finite.\n\n- Random variable “The number of clients arriving at a shopping mall in a day” cannot be modeled as a discrete uniform distribution. This is because the number of clients arriving at a shopping mall can be any positive integer, and each outcome is not equally likely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The number obtained when picking an integer between $0$ and $10$ at random” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166841 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b14560-29f9-58fc-ac65-5505987579fb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Situations That Can Be Modeled as a Discrete Uniform Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10973e79-c1b6-57b8-9851-6ae7106d412f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474996} {:answer/id #uuid "b6720f69-c55a-5a21-8a8c-910069c91507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6720f69-c55a-5a21-8a8c-910069c91507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474997} :answer-field/id #uuid "88439eea-1275-53b8-bdc6-f84f85c32054" :answer-field/key "The number obtained when picking a card from a set of cards numbered from $1$ to $12,$ at random." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801b11e7-8369-5538-8992-5653a6bcbd70" :answer/t