302eb51b923b1f193b72a.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4fcfc53-7279-50f5-90f1-bd8c9662d8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-110599" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}$ or ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II does not represent a subspace. There are vectors  $a=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$  in the subset for which ${a}_{1}>0$ and ${a}_{2}>0.$   But then\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}-{a}_{1} \\\\ -{a}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram III is a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is diagram III only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b1f26e-74e3-54dd-9a19-c2d7237c25a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453526} {:answer/id #uuid "4b07ac45-b4fe-591c-9ec8-4c6f325efb4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06b1f26e-74e3-54dd-9a19-c2d7237c25a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453526} :answer-field/id #uuid "02495e60-1290-53ef-9f15-de2782ac8189" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e976187d-1a3c-5254-ac57-00139179499a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453528} {:answer/id #uuid "bca2a77d-be2d-5162-9b1f-b5aabfcce26d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e976187d-1a3c-5254-ac57-00139179499a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453528} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b2dcd84-25cf-5410-9806-8fbaad74db0c" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R,$ we have $2\\cdot A\\in R.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af1f792c-ea17-539c-b803-70174e0206c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453530} {:answer/id #uuid "00f766d5-13c9-54cf-8c6a-17327b8856ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00f766d5-13c9-54cf-8c6a-17327b8856ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453531} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded477a5-7ff9-5d55-972d-d2753c0b4f0c" :answer-field/key "For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42098bc3-a0a9-510c-94ee-f777802bb49a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162666" :question/problem "Let $R$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\begin{bmatrix}{a}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ where $a\\in Z.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in R,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A\\in R.$” is false. For example,the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\in R,$ since $4={2}^{2}$ and $2\\in Z.$ However\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\notin R,\n$$\n\nbecause a negative number ($-4$) can't be a square.\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in R,$ we have $2\\cdot A\\in R.$” is false. For example, consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ from $R.$ Then, we have \n\n$$\n2\\cdot A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\notin R\n$$\n\nbecause the $22$-entry of $2\\cdot A$ is not equal to $1.$\n\n- Statement “For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.$” is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in R,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +1){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+{a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $A\\in R$ and $\\alpha \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha +1)A=\\alpha A+A.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Vector Addition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa6071c0-fff9-534e-9586-a01bcfff63d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453496} {:answer/id #uuid "4d3fbd9b-de38-5c14-bd68-eddf37af75ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d3fbd9b-de38-5c14-bd68-eddf37af75ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453497} :answer-field/id #uuid "868be7d6-6944-5cfb-b5c7-52473d4ca9b8" :answer-field/key "The exponential function $f(x)={e}^{x}\\in E$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183add14-81ee-5c40-a875-870eb4d49183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453498} {:answer/id #uuid "fcea62b3-8084-56ff-8cb4-1d53d269fe8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183add14-81ee-5c40-a875-870eb4d49183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453498} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2b928b0-206b-5ef1-be69-8e64cd6dfcb3" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x),g(x)\\in E$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in E.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47cf2934-bf49-5738-8cbd-42bb2111933c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453500} {:answer/id #uuid "fadcb3d1-7cde-5c14-83fa-f208111194de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47cf2934-bf49-5738-8cbd-42bb2111933c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453500} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ded8d53-6371-5429-8b4f-32fe142e8588" :answer-field/key "The set $E$ is closed under addition." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca37d526-e95e-5c72-ad4b-d05af7166afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-162394" :question/problem "Let $E$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ that satisfy $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The exponential function $f(x)={e}^{x}\\in E$” is true. Indeed, we have that\n\n$$\nf(0)={e}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f\\in E.$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in E$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in E.$” is false. For example, consider the function $f(x)=g(x)={e}^{x}\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n(f+g)(0)={e}^{0}+{e}^{0}=1+1=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)+g(x)\\notin E.$\n\n- Statement “The set $E$ is closed under addition” is false. Since statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in E$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in E.$” is false, $E$ is not closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The exponential function $f(x)={e}^{x}\\in E$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fcec0d8-ca03-5446-a42f-65d0ccddd584" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Quadrant of a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a8e17a0-daa3-5ce7-9699-c81f32093d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474502} {:answer/id #uuid "dcdf29b7-66c8-593e-b845-6514eb9e9b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a8e17a0-daa3-5ce7-9699-c81f32093d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474502} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fffa765-2a81-5787-b94f-54d3ea9dd2fd" :answer-field/key "It is in the fourth quadrant" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ee7af1-568a-504f-a7b5-3dc1b7f3487c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474504} {:answer/id #uuid "1aa59f6c-a796-5468-b924-eb34bdd4593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ee7af1-568a-504f-a7b5-3dc1b7f3487c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474504} :answer-field/id #uuid "115d02b4-a68c-542d-a036-9f4eff58e7c2" :answer-field/key "Its $x$-coordinate is $1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c90982-a31c-5706-b5d8-903cc7b07e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474506} {:answer/id #uuid "db66a6db-2f22-5d97-81b6-da2ae8fa5104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db66a6db-2f22-5d97-81b6-da2ae8fa5104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474507} :answer-field/id #uuid "34975eac-6fea-5e8a-8221-0a3c35d408d7" :answer-field/key "Its $y$-coordinate is $-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a" :question/math-academy-id "q-169184" :question/problem "![](images/92/928b00ea1ac59e758c4bc9e224d2d27e1c2149e31d0c5c3ab7673ee9abeae208.png)\n\nWhich of the following is true regarding the point $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $S$ is in the third quadrant, so statement “It is in the fourth quadrant” is false.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the point $S,$ we start at the origin, move $1$ units *left*, and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/f1/f150eac73755dc5f39b499b6ca0ba12624e4c27dd79e7207e11f6c88d04b596d.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $S$ are $(-1,-3).$ Hence, statement “Its $x$-coordinate is $1$” is false and statement “Its $y$-coordinate is $-3$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231429 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cac41120-247d-5821-b7f6-b342dbcf8f18" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14290d8c-e867-59b8-af1c-fccb11ec1cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474786} {:answer/id #uuid "ef81b3fc-df53-5633-a594-3d4f04f95619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14290d8c-e867-59b8-af1c-fccb11ec1cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474786} :answer-field/id #uuid "838696b9-c509-58f9-8a57-3688030a7f6e" :answer-field/key "$y$ $=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$ $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc17cc0-79a7-5ee7-b21f-ee6d25df87b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474788} {:answer/id #uuid "92aa028c-6b7c-580c-9ad9-b43fe721b886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dc17cc0-79a7-5ee7-b21f-ee6d25df87b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474788} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d3a8464-3e27-51fe-98f3-9d46f96ac2c0" :answer-field/key "$y$ $=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$ $-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa752ff5-8a8a-57e6-b3fb-ad9d131bd5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474790} {:answer/id #uuid "ee39a1b7-26b9-54e9-966d-579fbbb6a80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee39a1b7-26b9-54e9-966d-579fbbb6a80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474791} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b5e26ac-beb1-59bd-879a-7f19ce8bf81d" :answer-field/key "$y$ $=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ $-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "528870e0-56ba-55b5-a9bc-4fec3b9615fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-343753" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=-1$ and $D=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y$ $=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ $-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nOnly solution $y$ $=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ $-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ matches the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y$ $=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ $-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)$ $-\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a0526a2-d359-56c1-b909-e8be2980c9c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453398} {:answer/id #uuid "2318b4e8-9946-556e-9713-3affeb4a75e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2318b4e8-9946-556e-9713-3affeb4a75e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453399} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d2051c-cc4a-53b5-bfb1-613e54f12d04" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc7b6ede-9087-51f0-9391-ac769ed7b7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453400} {:answer/id #uuid "0417573f-1cae-56d6-9bb3-73ee34bed071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0417573f-1cae-56d6-9bb3-73ee34bed071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453401} :answer-field/id #uuid "82709fdc-0e50-5afa-adb3-4e8907d8c7af" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e4f8b1-a019-545a-9ccc-657e5b06d8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453402} {:answer/id #uuid "62da9a85-7410-5922-838a-f4f9375298c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6e4f8b1-a019-545a-9ccc-657e5b06d8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453402} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c95b926-8fa5-510c-b805-f0ecff86e55f" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0be806ce-1a6b-5ee1-964b-e362c3c8599e" :question/math-academy-id "q-140495" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =2(1)(3)+2(0)(1)+3(2)(-1) \\\\  & =6+0-6 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(1)(-9)+2(0)(-2)+3(2)(3) \\\\  & =-18+0+18 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}.$ Computing the inner product, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(3)(-9)+2(1)(-2)+3(-1)(3) \\\\  & =-54-4-9 \\\\  & =-67\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nSince ${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3},$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6f05695-5d5d-5e1b-bfad-77c51f81a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474374} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc309ff-eb8f-559c-b906-81545a54e0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc309ff-eb8f-559c-b906-81545a54e0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474375} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d94332b-01c8-5d93-bd36-59655b6dc3cf" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df48fe1-4c0e-5788-ae44-be72c3a42df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474376} {:answer/id #uuid "674b056b-93cf-5bbe-ae7e-6ce2c2c14c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df48fe1-4c0e-5788-ae44-be72c3a42df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474376} :answer-field/id #uuid "05746e78-6328-58c4-96d3-034fda58ec6d" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e78717-3155-5738-b52e-432f0cf2cf83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474378} {:answer/id #uuid "f66fe2c1-0155-5688-b8cc-b89a397d5048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f66fe2c1-0155-5688-b8cc-b89a397d5048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474379} :answer-field/id #uuid "453a25c3-916b-52ae-94c1-1cdb5d5d8d36" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f21c5fc-f92d-5b81-95e0-bb89748670fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140497" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=5{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =5(1)(-1)+(1)(7)+2(1)(-1) \\\\  & =-5+7-2 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}⊥̸{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =5(-1)(2)+(7)(0)+2(-1)(-5) \\\\  & =-10+0+10 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, computing the inner product $⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =5(1)(2)+(1)(0)+2(1)(-5) \\\\  & =10+0-10 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nAs a result, the set $S$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product”; “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4a33807-0dc5-58b8-9e96-d36c211cd17f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474200} {:answer/id #uuid "630190b1-87c4-5c43-bc91-504b4950f58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "630190b1-87c4-5c43-bc91-504b4950f58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474201} :answer-field/id #uuid "4790b87e-09c0-53d0-8040-c5d65661c89f" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2983d130-4a1c-5f7c-92f8-2b8f8ef9258b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474202} {:answer/id #uuid "5a01831f-984b-5618-8beb-6e5a83c9d9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a01831f-984b-5618-8beb-6e5a83c9d9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474203} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ee9bbc-f25e-576b-8ecb-a39f90ca2847" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c407a64-fdc1-57ce-9336-528dd1775a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474204} {:answer/id #uuid "b332a85e-6f82-5133-8e3a-be50909f94ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c407a64-fdc1-57ce-9336-528dd1775a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c2d9797-b732-51a2-940c-b09caf6ff041" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3a213f9-9ffe-56d7-a8aa-efb68c3978ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-104735" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $2$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(3(0))\\cdot (0+1)+(3(1))\\cdot (1+1) \\\\  & =6\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,{t}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{-1}+(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot ({t}^{2}-1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)^{2}-1)+(3(0))\\cdot ({0}^{2}-1)+(3(1))\\cdot ({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67683e7d-bf4f-5fdf-8fe5-df996c30e836" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Vectors Is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f67cf98-c041-56b4-b675-cd6608fe0e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475020} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa3734e-111b-53f2-8ebe-871dfb1f88e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f67cf98-c041-56b4-b675-cd6608fe0e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475020} :answer-field/id #uuid "17fd2243-0f57-5f80-9382-57761ade6958" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e85a7d43-b6d8-581b-9e5f-5f063c7c4b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475022} {:answer/id #uuid "b53eb6b7-af91-5d0b-8d68-a78f87a43b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53eb6b7-af91-5d0b-8d68-a78f87a43b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475023} :answer-field/id #uuid "623fd893-1fe0-5fbf-984e-f62b33160f96" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113ff175-e867-564a-8a13-cc2d64307b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475024} {:answer/id #uuid "72498a25-b060-53eb-8bae-7190cb5973bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72498a25-b060-53eb-8bae-7190cb5973bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475025} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac4eba3-941d-510f-b8db-bb23b5d39486" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1da803c-87de-5156-b3a7-d636001e9616" :question/math-academy-id "q-99637" :question/problem "$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors shown above. Given that the inner product in the vector space ${R}^{3}$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}⊥̸{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{2}⟩ & =2(2)(1)+3(-1)(1)+(1)(-1) \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{2}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{2},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(1)(0)+3(1)(1)+(-1)(3) \\\\  & =0+3-3 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, computing the inner product $⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{v}_{1},{v}_{3}⟩ & =2(2)(0)+3(-1)(1)+(1)(3) \\\\  & =0-3+3 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${v}_{1}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product.\nAs a result, the set $S$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}⊥{v}_{3}$ with respect to the given inner product”; “$S=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a5d11c2-4a7c-5fdc-a363-8a87b90db19e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4aa840c-676d-579d-907a-45c66e348cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454000} {:answer/id #uuid "5dfd99bd-c5b6-5c79-9329-4d49aaf5514c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dfd99bd-c5b6-5c79-9329-4d49aaf5514c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454001} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1077dc8-5cdf-55a4-9cf4-9f78c96894c1" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b075b0e-71d3-5492-a58e-181a0bd4a531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454002} {:answer/id #uuid "00552208-c5f0-56e1-9eb5-0d86c6ef59df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b075b0e-71d3-5492-a58e-181a0bd4a531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454002} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ff5afd-db04-5235-86fe-8c0c85c46c31" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\})=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee0c146-1417-5ad8-bd81-8ddd4be82e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454004} {:answer/id #uuid "80051909-7b26-58b5-b6ce-f8a75cd2c9ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80051909-7b26-58b5-b6ce-f8a75cd2c9ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454005} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98cc577-1407-5f32-81d7-2d8910452f11" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w\\})=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48a8881c-e6ac-54a2-9375-24bf5efbb3a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-79325" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a basis of a vector space $V$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that span $V.$ The dimension of $V$ is the number of vectors in any basis of $V$ (if such a basis exists). \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$” is true. Indeed, $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}.$ Moreover, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ are linearly independent vectors. So,  ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ is a basis of the span.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\})=2$ is false. Indeed, $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$, and we are told that ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span. Therefore, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\})=3$ (not $2$).\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w\\})=3$ is true. We are told that $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ This means that $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w\\}$ is completely spanned by the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ only. So, $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w\\})=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$”; $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w\\})=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7834049-c71e-58d4-8d98-c09398226feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437770} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e567b4-b8c2-531b-be4a-6a987225a67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7834049-c71e-58d4-8d98-c09398226feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437770} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6cf9cf-573c-532b-8b70-05635308acab" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d458576b-4e27-54ad-b0dd-01c8de1730f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437772} {:answer/id #uuid "95452bb7-2fca-5e83-88ee-5eea11dc8b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d458576b-4e27-54ad-b0dd-01c8de1730f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437772} :answer-field/id #uuid "15e08b68-718b-5246-ad09-cfa2adcaab8c" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨2y,\\,x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "937e30c9-442f-5622-a5d1-c5a8f129c9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437774} {:answer/id #uuid "8e713a4f-cc2e-59f3-b27f-a7992c92588d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e713a4f-cc2e-59f3-b27f-a7992c92588d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437775} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3f9770d-2312-582c-8540-7d2ef01450c3" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)$ $=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d67db6a-7337-599e-8ecc-26284642ae3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126574" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}⟩$ does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-{e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-2{e}^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨2y,\\,x⟩$ does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)$ $=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F(x,y)$ $=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21740e2f-600c-5a93-859b-56d238cd0e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437776} {:answer/id #uuid "2b9be679-baf3-5630-ae88-5b57cb494970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21740e2f-600c-5a93-859b-56d238cd0e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437776} :answer-field/id #uuid "b64b88b3-d28a-5b4a-a38b-7fe8543c12b6" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3},\\,{x}^{3}+1⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11bfb2c2-cc66-55c8-bec6-1505afc317a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437778} {:answer/id #uuid "8905b533-fda6-553c-b3a2-e716938166b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8905b533-fda6-553c-b3a2-e716938166b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437779} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfac5d71-e652-5d4b-8ce8-de5480e6fd0d" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438918} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5c9797-7316-5214-93dc-7545c27a4470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437780} {:answer/id #uuid "c013a325-7790-52f3-85d6-c6452b7b6dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c013a325-7790-52f3-85d6-c6452b7b6dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437781} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf7a35d-36f8-551d-abfc-0f58ffd44dd7" :answer-field/key "$F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c0dea55-217c-592d-9a6c-d305c8e67729" :question/math-academy-id "q-126575" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3},\\,{x}^{3}+1⟩$ does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{x}^{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field $F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$ gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$; $F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147430 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Simple Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace068e1-ab27-5034-9fdd-889739e4ddd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474972} {:answer/id #uuid "422799e5-23ee-5dc7-b632-76ffec3a5727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace068e1-ab27-5034-9fdd-889739e4ddd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474972} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8de985-d1e0-59b6-a5c0-3c4549c1a179" :answer-field/key "$y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t+{ϕ}_{1})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7496f0c4-2b46-5127-bfa7-c916b74f1f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474974} {:answer/id #uuid "bd89d55e-6590-5655-a89d-bbed83af8e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7496f0c4-2b46-5127-bfa7-c916b74f1f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474974} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7118b37-b721-5850-bd66-c32e1cbb4a4c" :answer-field/key "$y=R\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475413} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55c4ab68-5fcc-5325-b080-fc95a4cc450a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474976} {:answer/id #uuid "14f4fb0e-2d22-512b-ba94-b8520a2b3743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f4fb0e-2d22-512b-ba94-b8520a2b3743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474977} :answer-field/id #uuid "331f7cdf-6363-5525-b0c4-ce841a0d8619" :answer-field/key "$y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475414}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3951f87d-bb0f-5303-830e-d70693674542" :question/math-academy-id "q-94279" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=8\\,⟹\\,\\omega =2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)$\n\nTherefore, only statement $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\sqrt{2}t)$ could be used to represent  $y(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147432 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a459ec25-988e-5f91-8c25-2b7b81b6b6ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of a Mass-Spring System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4657c2-41bb-586d-a78c-c3631c9c62f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453910} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d30694-cffc-52bd-9c84-1a29c603a07e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5d30694-cffc-52bd-9c84-1a29c603a07e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453911} :answer-field/id #uuid "284e987f-668f-5073-82c4-6d1d6e4c9e59" :answer-field/key "The governing differential equation is ${y}^{″}+6y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454705} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b48675a-5e6c-57c1-a660-43f019d3237f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453912} {:answer/id #uuid "346f0314-00e3-50d1-bbdb-1f7dafaf2152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b48675a-5e6c-57c1-a660-43f019d3237f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453912} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21297d4-1bb6-52a0-9b68-8d0777902ab0" :answer-field/key "The frequency $f$ of the oscillation is $f=\\frac{3}{2\\pi }\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86a669b1-ce96-5301-9b01-0a42a18a7d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453914} {:answer/id #uuid "bae32439-f79c-53cf-9bc6-aa0048497990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86a669b1-ce96-5301-9b01-0a42a18a7d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453914} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9d225cd-6ad1-5a38-8acb-2295618fec83" :answer-field/key "The general solution can be expressed as $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t+ϕ),$ where $R$ is the amplitude and $ϕ$ is the phase." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a1d55e9e-973d-5821-a2d2-76fe96bd1d7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-64257" :question/problem "A particle of mass $5\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. The spring constant associated with the spring is $k=30\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.$ The position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds. \n\nIf the particle moves with simple harmonic motion, then which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement.\n\n- The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with simple harmonic motion (SHM) under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above equation gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{k}{m}y=0.\n$$\n\nComparing this to the SHM equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe see that\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{k}{m}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $k$ and $m$ gives\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{30}{5}=6\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{6}\n$$\n\nSo the governing differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+6y=0.\n$$\n\nHence, statement “The governing differential equation is ${y}^{″}+6y=0$” is true.\n\n- The frequency $f$ (measured in ${s}^{-1}$) is given by\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{1}{T}=\\frac{\\omega }{2\\pi },\n$$\n\nwhere $T$ is the period. So in our case, we have\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSo the frequency $f=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2\\pi }\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\nHence, statement “The frequency $f$ of the oscillation is $f=\\frac{3}{2\\pi }\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}$” is false.\n\n- The general solution for $y(t)$ can take one of three forms.\n\n1\\. $A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\n2\\. $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n3\\. $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\nWriting $\\omega =\\sqrt{6}$ and ${ϕ}_{1}=ϕ$ in form 3 gives\n\n$$\ny(t)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{6}t+ϕ).\n$$\n\nHence, statement “The general solution can be expressed as $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t+ϕ),$ where $R$ is the amplitude and $ϕ$ is the phase” is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The governing differential equation is ${y}^{″}+6y=0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b03ea89-5152-5ff4-813a-ca985d60ed5b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Orthogonality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1585707-1603-5a1b-af59-b5c138a9c074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453392} {:answer/id #uuid "4025897a-73f9-514f-9a24-860879c00094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4025897a-73f9-514f-9a24-860879c00094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453393} :answer-field/id #uuid "9169cb2e-f525-5cde-ad9b-110e6f63dc5a" :answer-field/key "$u⊥H,\\,$ where $H=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454446} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80b57557-ffd1-597f-9af9-6578ee6fa9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453394} {:answer/id #uuid "d94790ed-263f-5f65-b860-b1eed02e2ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80b57557-ffd1-597f-9af9-6578ee6fa9a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453394} :answer-field/id #uuid "4529a519-d7e4-51e4-907d-5d12e79418e7" :answer-field/key "$u⊥V,\\,$ where $V=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454447} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c7ea78-8c0f-597a-bff9-449b7300f6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453396} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca62772-2c0a-53cd-b01a-f279dc0c6b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06c7ea78-8c0f-597a-bff9-449b7300f6d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453396} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38bf924-51c4-568e-aabd-bffd18ea78d4" :answer-field/key "$u⊥W,\\,$ where $W=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adc7f30b-f5f4-5c71-84b9-9c4c7b9ab1ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-140464" :question/problem "For the vector $u=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $H,V$ and $W$ as $\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\},\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}\\}$, respectively.  \n\nNow, we have to compute the dot product between $u$ and the vectors in each set. \n\n- For the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =2\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot 1=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot 5=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =2\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-1)=4\\ne 0 & \\times  \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-5)=20\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸V.$\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =2\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 5=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =2\\cdot 10+1\\cdot (-5)+(-2)\\cdot 0=15\\ne 0 & \\times  \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{3} & =2\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-1)=4\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$u⊥H,\\,$ where $H=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\}$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ca7bae-c5f6-5f45-8005-39dc1d336efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474568} {:answer/id #uuid "ef16fdbd-534f-5a56-800d-2826d90b96e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef16fdbd-534f-5a56-800d-2826d90b96e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474569} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc71c1f9-a6aa-5adf-93aa-3ad18db40ff4" :answer-field/key "$x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276e0de2-7f03-5fe6-bac6-531d4adac97f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474570} {:answer/id #uuid "5d50814e-5f23-562d-83af-541b4e8b00c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276e0de2-7f03-5fe6-bac6-531d4adac97f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474570} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d43b3d-7d54-5b7b-a285-b49ab23b8daa" :answer-field/key "If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ or if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2787d35e-8a30-543b-9c6f-b675cf603e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474572} {:answer/id #uuid "c2395884-fbb1-5bc3-873c-dfa0f8ceb3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2395884-fbb1-5bc3-873c-dfa0f8ceb3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474573} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8fda271-0a88-58b9-887c-77bd606c8a3b" :answer-field/key "$x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0af36684-2b78-59f1-bddf-9a1297846d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183358" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ and if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$”; “$x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67fafecd-7387-5634-828c-573f1744befa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454214} {:answer/id #uuid "19a442fc-481d-58d8-9541-569ca4faf6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67fafecd-7387-5634-828c-573f1744befa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454214} :answer-field/id #uuid "5edb2284-a520-5008-b822-43d1ea474475" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is a $4\\times 2$ upper triangular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58652c7b-c953-5c9f-809b-80c39c943d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454216} {:answer/id #uuid "4713a280-f45c-5164-a1e2-ba8421f47c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4713a280-f45c-5164-a1e2-ba8421f47c73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454217} :answer-field/id #uuid "6346abcd-d6c5-5edc-add2-dd9c1ca312a0" :answer-field/key "The columns of $Q$ are unit vectors" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454858} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63f0bb0f-b477-52fc-b037-337d27feba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454218} {:answer/id #uuid "2a679340-6bec-5785-8c26-90181ea28dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63f0bb0f-b477-52fc-b037-337d27feba6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454218} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded79da7-007a-52a0-869d-714c07ace673" :answer-field/key "$R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b19eecb-3ecc-5584-a617-4bf8675e0b01" :question/math-academy-id "q-95917" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $4\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is a $4\\times 2$ upper triangular matrix” is false. $Q$ should be a $4\\times 2$ matrix, but is not necessarily upper triangular.\n\n- Statement “The columns of $Q$ are unit vectors” is true. Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis, they are unit vectors.\n\n- Statement “$R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix” is false. $R$ must be a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The columns of $Q$ are unit vectors” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1caac6a-22d0-5cd7-9db0-e0140ddcd909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454220} {:answer/id #uuid "b926ed9f-ad1b-50f1-813b-bcebdb95283d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1caac6a-22d0-5cd7-9db0-e0140ddcd909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454220} :answer-field/id #uuid "49fdd229-50f4-564f-b524-d4bd1740977e" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is a square matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216e1a0c-f709-5bea-bcc9-fad94ad25e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454222} {:answer/id #uuid "1818db3a-f150-5c54-a87a-f9f270c059d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1818db3a-f150-5c54-a87a-f9f270c059d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454223} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad557eb7-0609-5346-a166-6ae7a67329b7" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)$ is spanned by the columns of $Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "816aef43-e159-58e4-a4c1-b677dcb3fedb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454224} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d01fa8-8a2f-5f4b-8c5a-b721f1c70aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d01fa8-8a2f-5f4b-8c5a-b721f1c70aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454225} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c94478-bfe1-5ec1-83de-46a4b043e55c" :answer-field/key "$R$ is a square matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71004f41-ae2f-50fd-9fdc-88ec92c18337" :question/math-academy-id "q-95919" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of a $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is a square matrix” is false. $Q$ should be an $m\\times n$ matrix, so $Q$ is not necessarily a square matrix.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is spanned by the columns of $Q$” is true.  Since the columns of $Q$ form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A),$ they must span $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\n- Statement “$R$ is a square matrix” is true. Indeed, $R$ must be an $m\\times n$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$\\text{Col}(A)$ is spanned by the columns of $Q$”; “$R$ is a square matrix” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133864 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1304189f-61ac-53c5-9b09-8e365f763136" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Dimensions of Factors in a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9947571e-4699-552c-a3f8-cdb4afcb91b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454226} {:answer/id #uuid "f994e63a-bbab-5e72-b8ec-01fb36bba58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f994e63a-bbab-5e72-b8ec-01fb36bba58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454227} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec5b35fe-24dc-5c9f-94a8-2e607d7345ed" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is an $8\\times 4$ matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454863} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b70d1295-4456-519c-b854-3cea919fcd6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454228} {:answer/id #uuid "107f980f-794e-512a-b1a5-3423d808c90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70d1295-4456-519c-b854-3cea919fcd6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454228} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ffc576b-19a5-5b8d-861f-1562b307f361" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454864} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fde51b-666c-555f-a5c5-56cb4c845f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454230} {:answer/id #uuid "4da6d724-00ba-5715-9f39-d7456f67bcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4da6d724-00ba-5715-9f39-d7456f67bcff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454231} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadd3e43-e943-5264-873b-86eaa5bb28e1" :answer-field/key "$R$ is an upper triangular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6266ee7-76af-56d5-9957-fa402398ddd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95923" :question/problem "Given that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of an $8\\times 4$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $A=QR$ is a  QR factorization of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n$$\n{A}_{m\\times n}={Q}_{m\\times n}\\times {R}_{n\\times n},\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $Q$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix whose columns form an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\n- $R$ is an $n\\times n$ upper triangular matrix\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$Q$ is an $8\\times 4$ matrix” is true. Indeed, $Q$ must be an $8\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement “$R$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix” is false. $R$ should be a $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement “$R$ is an upper triangular matrix” is true. Indeed $R$ must be an upper triangular matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$Q$ is an $8\\times 4$ matrix”; “$R$ is an upper triangular matrix” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9434ee35-97a1-5285-97bd-642508f58883" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474768} {:answer/id #uuid "2e62f471-e501-527c-a2bf-b58c36ed0de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e62f471-e501-527c-a2bf-b58c36ed0de8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474769} :answer-field/id #uuid "f52c9065-8b6f-5163-be58-9a1c7fadbe10" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee5d6baf-53f3-5f60-82f6-8b26db329f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474770} {:answer/id #uuid "87258704-04de-53fe-86be-3991a51c9d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87258704-04de-53fe-86be-3991a51c9d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474771} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f5919f8-4a8b-57fc-ba5e-3d0f046a50c8" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475311} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a4f9e18-0783-5aa4-ba7f-a403d553756b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474772} {:answer/id #uuid "b9af53cc-7fb3-530b-a444-9b33c32f55d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9af53cc-7fb3-530b-a444-9b33c32f55d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474773} :answer-field/id #uuid "da939024-b939-5a26-a4f7-b9817e50d965" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248767b0-4e8f-59a2-a18a-6d7a3f7d1129" :question/math-academy-id "q-334262" :question/problem "$$\n4{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+6x{y}^{′}-2y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x).$ Notice that $\\frac{1}{x}={x}^{-1},$ so we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right)+6x\\left(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) & =0 \\\\ (\\frac{8}{x}-\\frac{6}{x}-\\frac{2}{x}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$” is true. First, we find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x).$ Notice that $\\sqrt{x}={x}^{\\frac{1}{2}},$ so we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2})+6x(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2})-2\\sqrt{x} & =0 \\\\ (-{x}^{1/2}+3{x}^{1/2}-2{x}^{1/2}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$” is true. Both ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of the equation. To check if these functions are linearly independent, we compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-1} & {x}^{1/2} \\\\ -{x}^{-2} & \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={x}^{-1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-{x}^{1/2}\\cdot (-{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2}+{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the  Wronskian is not identically $0$ on $(0,\\infty ),$ the functions are linearly independent. Hence, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$”; “${y}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is a solution to the equation for $x>0.$”; “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation on $(0,\\infty ).$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e66005fe-df33-590a-9d9c-91947cd4a608" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Fundamental Sets of Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bacd32ae-566a-595f-ae61-c7390064179f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474762} {:answer/id #uuid "af9b7df9-824a-5976-8ef0-0ed97e33de24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bacd32ae-566a-595f-ae61-c7390064179f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474762} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b52e612-ea71-5a2e-a81c-18901ac0011f" :answer-field/key "${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9146691-1ccc-57f9-88b9-54805a3f76b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474764} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb64cb4-e2ff-50e2-a176-9905722d9d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb64cb4-e2ff-50e2-a176-9905722d9d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474765} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f934a8-f5e6-5690-a1d4-2746d5ccf5fa" :answer-field/key "${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475308} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25a7c82-ba97-5324-83d9-8843be6f251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474766} {:answer/id #uuid "97e7e003-0f8d-59ae-a1f3-79ac064de7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25a7c82-ba97-5324-83d9-8843be6f251d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474766} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb9f336-1bf0-5e57-b4b7-e8e56b5843aa" :answer-field/key "The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8005871f-5013-58a1-b9ee-7ef831d491ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-334257" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-12y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that to determine whether $y(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute $y$ and its derivatives into the equation. \n\nLet's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}$ is a solution to the equation” is false. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{12}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\left(\\frac{12}{{x}^{5}}\\right)+2x\\left(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\right)-12\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\right) & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}} & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}(x)$ is not a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation” is true. We find the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =6x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(6x)+2x(3{x}^{2})-12({x}^{3}) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}(x)$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- Statement “The functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation” is false. Since ${y}_{1}(x)$ is not a solution of the given differential equation, ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ don't form a set of fundamental solutions to the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{3}$ is a solution to the equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e75041c-d0be-5db2-a0db-7c2c2b57b44e" :knowledge-point/title "Defining the Gamma Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d3ee888-ad53-54fd-b343-fe6d7467993b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474236} {:answer/id #uuid "13309c56-de8d-541c-a9b9-d64bacc69c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13309c56-de8d-541c-a9b9-d64bacc69c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474237} :answer-field/id #uuid "55357c0e-8442-539c-a2ac-0b8d9168a5e9" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46b17db1-3dae-59e5-90f2-f8086dd367db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474238} {:answer/id #uuid "87817e80-cdc4-5f99-b785-8dc24554f274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87817e80-cdc4-5f99-b785-8dc24554f274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474239} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4b8c22-2a7d-5614-bb76-1bdd501394ac" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "946ef7c6-6523-56ec-ba6b-6b5367226abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474240} {:answer/id #uuid "38796f5a-37c3-5e26-8904-8a488026bd3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "946ef7c6-6523-56ec-ba6b-6b5367226abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474240} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e1408d-a412-5bd8-99d6-c8b390cde190" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d9f5142-140d-5b22-b957-299741979b12" :question/math-academy-id "q-107888" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$ matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$ matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$ does *not* match the definition. The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t$; ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e75041c-d0be-5db2-a0db-7c2c2b57b44e" :knowledge-point/title "Defining the Gamma Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a04469a3-7f07-5d95-b3ed-53d23583c001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474224} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6c6c36-9ef3-5b50-bace-e5373e8e111d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a04469a3-7f07-5d95-b3ed-53d23583c001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474224} :answer-field/id #uuid "95800a72-af37-5e50-87d8-4d778088679e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "659a0c2a-7edb-5bbe-88f2-3b9b2eff819b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474226} {:answer/id #uuid "3791b2ef-5b11-5cc9-baae-03f8088dbaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "659a0c2a-7edb-5bbe-88f2-3b9b2eff819b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474226} :answer-field/id #uuid "35830ead-3b62-5793-9b43-dd92136145db" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f97df9c-3d9f-5677-84fc-d5df4d829f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474228} {:answer/id #uuid "444410c8-abc9-5f03-b73e-a36a15972c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "444410c8-abc9-5f03-b73e-a36a15972c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474229} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f7efb2-3828-5436-ab69-9709be08f7b3" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2346f7c5-c1ac-509c-ac43-d1a23908e3df" :question/math-academy-id "q-107833" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals are equivalent to $Γ(z)$ for $\\text{Re}(z)>0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the definition of the gamma function:\n\n$$\nΓ(z)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\text{Re}(z)>0.\n$$\n\nWith this definition in mind, let's consider each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{z-1}}\\,\\text{d}t$ does *not* match the definition. The integrand $\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{t}^{z-1}}$ is not equivalent to that shown in the definition.\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{t}^{z-1}}{{e}^{t}}\\,\\text{d}t$ does *not* match the definition.  The lower bound of integration does not match that given in the definition.\n\n- Integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}$ matches the definition:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{z-1}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t=Γ(z)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}t}{{t}^{1-z}{e}^{t}}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432690 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172066 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e75041c-d0be-5db2-a0db-7c2c2b57b44e" :knowledge-point/title "Defining the Gamma Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd8b7241-1245-5d5b-a271-d1237489a963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474212} {:answer/id #uuid "8b991a22-640f-50f4-9d9d-a048962ad7e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b991a22-640f-50f4-9d9d-a048962ad7e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474213} :answer-field/id #uuid "0463b58c-d01d-596e-9ffa-9b8eac7f3680" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-t}}{{t}^{1-z}}\\,\\text{d}t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3131c2f5-825f-5550-a34f-fef8ce169331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474214} {:answer/id #uuid "f4471068-8be8-5bd6-9aaa-3a50e98b819a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604